    "status": "submitted",
    "answer": "Requirements apply at the time of award. The applicant must be a for-profit small business with a U.S. place of business. It must operate primarily in the United States or significantly contribute to the U.S. economy through taxes or use of American products, materials, or labor. It must meet applicable U.S. ownership and control requirements; under the standard rule, more than 50% is directly owned and controlled by eligible U.S. citizens or permanent residents, qualifying small businesses, or an allowable combination. Including affiliates, it generally may have no more than 500 employees, subject to SBA size and affiliation rules. A nonprofit cannot directly receive an SBIR award. Certain participating agencies may make SBIR awards under an exception for firms majority-owned by multiple venture-capital operating companies, hedge funds, or private-equity firms. [SRC-1; SRC-2]",
